ation","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Didactics of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Carlsen","key":"louisemeierpau","last":"Louise Meier","name":"Louise Meier, Carlsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Britta Eyrich","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"ac53e617-ed92-4aaf-a2cc-0771bea7cad4","name":"Jessen, Britta Eyrich","orcid":"0000-0003-0612-7558","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-416a3798-bd06-48ee-8c0d-31d07912608e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"WHAT ARE THE POTENTIAL RELATIONS BETWEEN MATHEMATICAL MODELLING AND COMPUTING EDUCATION – THE CASE OF SIMULATIONS","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730940","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Computer algebra systems (CAS) are an integrated part of teaching and learning mathematics in upper secondary school, which has resulted in more and more teachers in lower secondary school considering implementing CAS. However, in lower secondary school pupils are introduced to elementary algebra, and CAS-use therefor does not seem as obvious. Indeed, some questions remain, including the following: 1) How is CAS compatible with the current approach to teaching school algebra, when the dominant tasks are solving equations? 2) How can teacher education support preservice teachers in implementing CAS when little well-established knowledge exists about CAS-based teaching? This thesis comprises of a literature review and three papers. The first paper considers the epistemic value of the current paper-and-pencil approach to teaching algebra and how this is influenced by a naïve implementation of CAS. The second paper, on the other hand, studies how CAS can lever the pupils’ knowledge and practice for manipulating and solving equations. The third study examines formats for supporting preservice teachers in developing and formulating knowledge and practice for implementing CAS in the teaching and learning of school algebra.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Carlsen, Louise Meier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712862"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"teachers practice and knowledge on school algebra with cas","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ind.ku.dk/publikationer/inds_skriftserie/nr.-582021-teachers-practice-and-knowledge-on-school-algebra-with-cas/Skriftserie_nr_58.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712862","ids":["ku-1225c0c4-714e-4e79-be05-6f12099ce05b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A89C5F89E68E9404D7678F53294D9D3C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ind.ku.dk/publikationer/inds_skriftserie/nr.-582021-teachers-practice-and-knowledge-on-school-algebra-with-cas/Skriftserie_nr_58.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Didactics of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Meier","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","locid":"70d1b2b6-b2e7-4425-ab76-862494ce5c48","name":"Carlsen, Louise Meier","orcid":"0000-0003-3987-9350","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"154","publisher":"Department of Science Education, University of Copenhagen, Denmark","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1225c0c4-714e-4e79-be05-6f12099ce05b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Teachers’ Practice and Knowledge on School Algebra with CAS","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712862","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We are interested in the potentials and pitfalls of introducing computer algebra systems in lower secondary school, investigating the case of the Faroese Islands. In order to identify what algebraic knowledge is tested in the final written exam in mathematics after the ninth grade, and how this would change if computer algebra systems were allowed at that exam, we analyse all exam exercises from the past 10 years in terms of the techniques required to solve the exercises both with and without symbolic tools. The comparison suggests that fundamental algebraic structures may not be learned if students consistently use computer algebra systems for the tasks given in the exam.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Carlsen, Louise Meier"],"cuid":["S02-089.29-704511"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"country":["Faroe Islands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of the Faroe Islands"],"keyword":["algebraic knowledge","exam exercises","praxeological analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what algebraic knowledge may not be learned with cas a praxeological analysis of faroese exam exercises","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23925/1983-3156.2019v21i4p085-099","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.29-704511","ids":["itu-036fd8fc-e993-44c3-9809-9d9a028d3684","ku-4107e7f8-5077-44b3-a4f3-3f280c93576b"],"keyword":["algebraic knowledge","exam exercises","praxeological analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DB0EE8BC9DE452526E793C3B8587A60B"],"oa_link":[{"access"